tes human flourishing and the art of living well. It is clear vision of awareness of Buddhist Meditation among the students of GBU." Another bullet: "This course will be very helpful to personality development through mindfulness meditation technique in the students’ careers. Personality trait and mindfulness are associated with a way we understand ourselves and those around us to be able to demonstrate skills to react in society peacefully." Next: "These skills are, for example, working with others, solving problems, making decisions, and adapting to change." Then: "Bodhi Mindfulness Meditation is the only course on campus that provides an opportunity to learn about, discuss, reflect on, and practices various forms of meditations and mindfulness and loving kindness." Another bullet: "The course provides, at a minimum, an hour each week for students to come and learn about not only what various types of meditation and mindfulness are, but especially why they’re important and how to apply them to daily life." Last bullet: "Everyone is welcome to share insight, stories, thoughts, etc. as the group is a learning experience for everyone. Each meeting is a chance for students relax for an hour at the beginning of the week – to center themselves and walk away with a new perspective, a sense of connectedness, and maybe a bit of wisdom."\n\nThen there's a section titled "Bodhi Meditation Course/Programme Schedule". It's a table with columns: S.No., Days/Month, Types of Course/Programmes, Time Duration, Practitioners. The rows are: 1. Every Monday & Thursday, Bodhi Meditation course for beginners, 5.00-6.00 PM, GBU Students only. 2. Every Friday, Advance Course on Bodhi Meditation for Trainers, 4.00-5.00 PM, BMC Members only. 3. Every 2nd Sunday of the month, Basic Mindfulness Meditation Practices, 8.00-9.00 AM, GBU Family members. 4. Every 4th Saturday of the month, Day Workshop on Bodhi Meditation with Sub-Theme: Motivation: Effective Study & Student Career, 2.00-5.30 PM, 